/**
 * @mainpage libjpl API
 *
 * Choose a task below to jump directly to a function's documentation.
 * Each entry describes its arguments, return value, and usage notes.
 * For a full type and constant listing, see the public header pages.
 *
 * ## Opening and inspecting files
 * - @ref jpl_open "jpl_open()" - Open a DE binary with file I/O.
 * - @ref jpl_open_mmap "jpl_open_mmap()" - Open a DE binary with memory mapping.
 * - @ref jpl_ephemeris_clone "jpl_ephemeris_clone()" - Clone a handle for concurrent readers.
 * - @ref jpl_close "jpl_close()" - Release a handle.
 * - @ref jpl_get_header "jpl_get_header()" - Inspect file coverage and metadata.
 * - @ref jpl_read_constants "jpl_read_constants()" - Read the constants record.
 * - @ref jpl_get_constant_name "jpl_get_constant_name()" - Read any constant name, including names past the first 400.
 * - @ref jpl_read_record "jpl_read_record()" - Read a raw coefficient record.
 * - @ref jpl_record_count "jpl_record_count()" - Count coefficient records.
 *
 * ## State calculations
 * - @ref jpl_get_state "jpl_get_state()" - Interpolate a relative state.
 * - @ref jpl_get_state_lighttime "jpl_get_state_lighttime()" - Apply light-time correction.
 * - @ref jpl_get_lighttime_solution "jpl_get_lighttime_solution()" - Get the atomic light-time solution (state, observer, delay, emission).
 * - @ref jpl_apply_aberration "jpl_apply_aberration()" - Apply stellar aberration (solar term included when Sun distance > 0).
 *
 * ## Time and frames
 * - @ref jpl_has_tt_tdb "jpl_has_tt_tdb()" - Check for file-provided time corrections.
 * - @ref jpl_get_tt_minus_tdb "jpl_get_tt_minus_tdb()" - Interpolate a file-provided time correction.
 * - @ref jpl_tt_to_tdb "jpl_tt_to_tdb()" - Convert TT to TDB.
 * - @ref jpl_tdb_to_tt "jpl_tdb_to_tt()" - Convert TDB to TT.
 * - @ref jpl_icrs_to_ecliptic "jpl_icrs_to_ecliptic()" - Rotate an ICRS state to the ecliptic.
 * - @ref jpl_frame_rotation_matrix "jpl_frame_rotation_matrix()" - Get the ecliptic-to-ICRS matrix.
 * - @ref jpl_frame_context_create "jpl_frame_context_create()" - Create a cached ecliptic-to-ICRS frame context.
 * - @ref jpl_frame_context_destroy "jpl_frame_context_destroy()" - Destroy a frame context.
 * - @ref jpl_frame_context_rotate_vector "jpl_frame_context_rotate_vector()" - Rotate a vector using a frame context.
 * - @ref jpl_frame_context_rotate_state "jpl_frame_context_rotate_state()" - Rotate a state vector using a frame context.
 *
 * ## Convenience helpers
 * - @ref jpl_planet_position "jpl_planet_position()" - Compute an apparent planet position.
 * - @ref jpl_moon_position "jpl_moon_position()" - Compute an apparent Moon position.
 * - @ref jpl_apparent_ecliptic_position "jpl_apparent_ecliptic_position()" - Query geocentric apparent longitude, latitude, and range.
 * - @ref jpl_au_per_day_to_km_per_s "jpl_au_per_day_to_km_per_s()" - Convert velocity units.
 * - @ref jpl_km_to_au "jpl_km_to_au()" - Convert distance units.
 *
 * ## Core types
 * - @ref jpl_date "jpl_date" - Two-part Julian date (`{hi, lo}`).
 * - @ref jpl_state "jpl_state" - Six-component position and velocity state vector.
 * - @ref jpl_lighttime_solution "jpl_lighttime_solution" - Atomic light-time solution value.
 * - @ref jpl_frame_context "jpl_frame_context" - Opaque cached frame conversion context.
 *
 * ## Status and errors
 * - @ref jpl_status_string "jpl_status_string()" - Describe a status code.
 *
 * The public headers are @c jpl.h, @c jpl_frames.h, and @c jpl_convenience.h.
 */
